Test_termdebug_evaluate() checks the most recent message immediately after
asking gdb to evaluate an expression.  Under the Solaris screen-based terminal
harness, gdb can print the intermediate "expr: ..." prompt before the evaluated
result reaches Vim messages.  Slower SPARC runs can still need more than a
short wait there, so wait longer after Evaluate so the test checks the actual
expression result instead of the prompt.

Test_termdebug_toggle_break() creates several duplicate breakpoints and then
toggles them off.  Wait after each Break command so the signs for all duplicate
breakpoints are registered before ToggleBreak removes them.

--- vim-9.2.0564/src/testdir/test_plugin_termdebug.vim
+++ vim-9.2.0564/src/testdir/test_plugin_termdebug.vim
@@ -387,13 +387,13 @@
 
   " Evaluate an expression
   Evaluate n
-  call term_wait(gdb_buf)
+  call term_wait(gdb_buf, 2000)
   call assert_equal(execute('1messages')->trim(), '"n": 7')
   Evaluate argc
-  call term_wait(gdb_buf)
+  call term_wait(gdb_buf, 2000)
   call assert_equal(execute('1messages')->trim(), '"argc": 1')
   Evaluate isprime(n)
-  call term_wait(gdb_buf)
+  call term_wait(gdb_buf, 2000)
   call assert_equal(execute('1messages')->trim(), '"isprime(n)": 1')
 
   wincmd t
@@ -756,8 +756,11 @@
 
   " Remove multiple break points
   execute "Break"
+  call term_wait(gdb_buf, 400)
   execute "Break"
+  call term_wait(gdb_buf, 400)
   execute "Break"
+  call term_wait(gdb_buf, 400)
   execute "Break"
   call term_wait(gdb_buf, 400)
   execute "ToggleBreak"
